n)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta2 - Fedora Linux 43 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (nvidia; 580.119.02) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600XT 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.50 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\npoint of popup notifications is to quickly draw users attention to information, and give them context, and/or give opportunity to take action.\n\nusually it give user context about current state, warns about possible/expected misbehaviour, that could save them lots of time, otherwise trying to figure out what's going on on their own.\n\nit's important that such notifications draw attention, (as it can save lots of time) in current design it's very easy to miss out on those notifications when some docks/tabs are open (see images below)\n\nit could be simple fix such as changing color so it stands out from active theme, adding shadow or border around notification...\n\nand even better, most users on desktop have intuition/are used to seeing those kinds of notifications aligned to one of the corner of monitor, most of the time right bottom/top sides, currently in godot it's aligned to notifications bell icon, that is on the bottom right side but not aligned to the edge of window, it could be moved to the edge, that would further improve visibility.\n\n<img width=\"1043\" height=\"145\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ccc4bda-88d2-4cca-aa4b-2e4dbf45d0b9\" />\n\n<img width=\"1247\" height=\"287\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56ebe90c-6c5c-482d-86ca-2998d27adbe9\" />\n\n<img width=\"1247\" height=\"287\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c8cc2405-caad-4611-9630-d868382cc32b\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avat